{
  "character": "本",
  "summary": {
    "text": "本 points to the root or base of a tree. It takes 木, “tree,” and adds a short horizontal mark near the bottom to highlight the roots. This gives the abstract senses “origin,” “source,” and “basis” a concrete image: the part from which the tree grows.",
    "evidence_ids": [
      "E1",
      "E2",
      "E4",
      "E6"
    ]
  },
  "history": [
    {
      "text": "The Shuowen describes the bottom of the tree as 本 and notes the added line underneath. The extra stroke acts as a pointer within the tree picture; its position tells the reader which part to attend to.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "E3"
      ]
    }
  ],
